Z||000005||GT Bastard||03-29-2001||01:41 PM||||Thanks Trav... I didn't expect to keep up with him at all.  The first run he bogged his car off the line and gave me an easy lead.  The kicker is that he never caught up!  This can be partially attributed to the fact that his car wasn't running tip-top.  His car seemed to run pretty rough, and the manifold was glowing bright orange after both runs.  Then again, a stock VR4 only makes 195hp/203lbs torque in a fairly heavy car...  The second run I accidentally dumped my clutch at 3,000 rpm and burned all the way through 1st(we were going slightly downhill and I was trying to keep it from rolling), then scratched it bad into second.  His launch was impressive this time(he built-up boost with the e-brake on.)  He pulled past me with all four tires smoking.  I ended up about 3 or 4 car lenghts behind him the whole way(1/4 mile or maybe a bit longer.)  All things considered his car is probably a bit quicker through the quarter, but it's damn close.  It'll be interesting to see how much faster he is when he gets his mechanical issues worked out... But by that time, I should be cruizing in a forged 2.8 on giggle-gas.... Bwahahaha...  Just to clarify, the guy was pretty cool about the race(though nobody watching the race expected the Fiero to hang with him at all.) ||||reg||1
